      "side": 1,
      "message": "A couple observations here:\n\n1. This is very similar to the logic in pd_is_mode_discovered_for_svid. I think that logic could probably be made reusable for this purpose. The discovery state accessors are a bit messy right now, and you\u0027d have to change them around so that you had something like pd_get_mode_vdo_for_svid. I don\u0027t think this should be a significant amount of work.\n\n2. A function like this should really be in usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c. It looks like the only reason it isn\u0027t is so that TCPMv1 can implement its own version using the pd_cable structure. I think it would be cleaner to put this version, which is essentially TCPM-version-agnostic, in a generic location.\n\nIn summary, if you could implement this generically (to both SVID and TCPM version) in usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c, that would be great.\n\n(I have a TODO to clean up the discovery state API in usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c. My apologies for its current condition.)",
      "revId": "db10f607bf0d9d21ef950d67c9f28df6246080b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
